+<section id="s3" class="question"><h2><span>3.</span> Research question</h2>
+<div class="content"><p class="">With the answer generator fixed, which pipeline additions improve answer quality and page-level citation precision and recall, and where do these objectives conflict?</p>
+</div></section>
 
-<section aria-labelledby="results-title">
- <div class="section-title"><span class="num">03</span><h2 id="results-title">Results</h2><span class="english">R0 to R6 on the mixed corpus</span></div>
+<section id="s4" class=""><h2><span>4.</span> Our Contribution</h2>
+<div class="content"><p class="">We build a Legal RAG pipeline and provide an empirical comparison of seven cumulative configurations on 30 documents and 100 questions. By adding components sequentially while keeping the answer generator fixed, we measure changes in answer quality and page-level citation precision and recall across stages of document processing, retrieval, reranking, answer processing, and citation selection.</p>
+</div></section>
 
- <figure><img class="chart" src="../results/pipeline-metrics.svg" alt="Q for R0 to R6: 46.2, 63.2, 49.8, 74.6, 84.4, 84.4, 84.4%. Precision: 7.6, 11.2, 14.7, 22.2, 27.1, 27.1, 61.8%. Recall: 38.5, 61.6, 52.9, 72.7, 78.9, 78.9, 74.7%."/></figure>
- <div class="grid detail-grid">
-  <div><h3>OCR recovers performance on scanned documents</h3><img class="ocr" src="../results/ocr-control.svg" alt="Answer quality: original corpus R0 65.4%; mixed corpus R0 46.2%; mixed corpus with OCR R1 63.2%."><p>Converting 10 documents into synthetic scans reduces answer quality from 65.4% to 46.2%. OCR restores most of this loss, reaching 63.2%.</p></div>
-  <div><h3>Hypothesis evaluation</h3>
-   <p class="hyp-row"><strong>H1 · Partially supported.</strong> Multiple scales alone reduce Q; lexical retrieval and reranking improve Q and recall.</p>
-   <p class="hyp-row"><strong>H2 · Supported.</strong> OCR restores most of the loss caused by removing the text layer.</p>
-   <p class="hyp-row"><strong>H3 · Supported with a trade-off.</strong> Precision rises from 27.1% to 61.8%; recall falls from 78.9% to 74.7% (−4.2 pp).</p>
-   <div class="limitations">
-    <h3>Limitations</h3>
-    <p>one DIFC corpus and 100 questions; one run per condition with no significance testing; LLM-based evaluation of free-text answers.</p>
-   </div>
-  </div>
- </div>
- <div class="conclusion">
-  <h3>Conclusion</h3>
-  <p>Legal RAG should be designed as a multi-stage pipeline: OCR improves robustness to unreadable PDFs, hybrid retrieval and reranking improve answer quality, and post-answer citation selection improves citation precision. However, citation selection introduces a precision–recall trade-off, so answer quality and citation quality should be optimized and evaluated separately.</p>
- </div>
-</section>
+<section id="s5" class=""><h2><span>5.</span> Hypothesis</h2>
+<div class="content"><div class="hyp h1"><h3>H1 — Retrieval</h3>
+<p class="">Combining multiple text granularities, semantic and lexical retrieval, and relevance reranking will improve answer quality and evidence retrieval compared with a simple semantic-retrieval baseline.</p>
+</div><div class="hyp h2"><h3>H2 — Robustness to scanned documents</h3>
+<p class="">Recovering text from scan-like legal documents will reduce the performance loss caused by the absence of a machine-readable text layer.</p>
+</div><div class="hyp h3"><h3>H3 — Citation attribution</h3>
+<p class="">Selecting source pages after answer generation will produce a more focused citation set without substantially reducing the coverage of relevant evidence.</p>
+</div></div></section>
+</div>
+<div class="col center">
+<section id="s6" class=""><h2><span>6.</span> Data and Methods</h2>
+<div class="content"><h3>Data</h3>
+<p class="">30 DIFC legal PDFs (590 pages), 100 questions, including 70 structured-answer and 30 free-text questions. Reference source pages are available for 95 questions. For the scan-robustness test, 10 of the 30 documents (107 pages) were converted into synthetic scans: each page was rasterised as an image and its machine-readable text layer was removed.</p>
+<h3 class="subhead">Pipeline</h3>
+<p class="">Starting from a simple baseline, we add one capability at a time. Each variant includes all previous additions.</p>
+<div class="baseline"><h3>R0 · Baseline</h3>
+<div class="flow"><div><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-file"/></svg><strong>PDF text<br><span>300-token passages</span></strong></div><div><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-search"/></svg><strong>Semantic retrieval<span class="model">Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B</span></strong></div><div><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-answer"/></svg><strong>Generate answer<span class="model">GPT-5.4-mini</span></strong></div><div><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-file"/></svg><strong>Answer +<br>retrieved pages</strong></div></div></div><div class="stages"><div class="phase doc">Document processing</div><div class="phase retr">Retrieval</div><div class="phase ans single">Answering</div><div class="phase cit single">Citations</div><div class="stage doc"><h3>R1 · Read scans</h3>
+<p class="">Convert scanned pages into searchable text</p>
+<svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-scan"/></svg><p class="tech">PP-OCRv5</p>
+</div><div class="stage doc"><h3>R2 · Multiple scales</h3>
+<p class="">Represent evidence at multiple scales</p>
+<svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-layers"/></svg><p class="tech">Pages, sections, clauses, microchunks, tables</p>
+</div><div class="stage retr"><h3>R3 · Find exact terms too</h3>
+<p class="">Combine semantic and exact-word search</p>
+<svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-search"/></svg><p class="tech">BM25 + RRF</p>
+</div><div class="stage retr"><h3>R4 · Prioritize better evidence</h3>
+<p class="">Move the most relevant passages to the top</p>
+<svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-rank"/></svg><p class="tech">Qwen3-Reranker</p>
+</div><div class="stage ans"><h3>R5 · Check the answer</h3>
+<p class="">Normalize and validate the expected answer type</p>
+<svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-check"/></svg><p class="tech">Typed schema</p>
+</div><div class="stage cit"><h3>R6 · Refine citations</h3>
+<p class="">Keep only pages that support the final answer</p>
+<svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-link"/></svg><p class="tech">Supporting-chunk references</p>
+</div></div><p class="fixed"><strong>Answer generation:</strong> A fixed GPT-5.4-mini configuration is used across variants, so changes in performance reflect modifications to the surrounding pipeline rather than a change of the generating LLM.</p>
+</div></section>
 
