+<li>Butler, A. R., &amp; Butler, U. (2026). Legal RAG Bench: an end-to-end benchmark for legal RAG. arXiv preprint arXiv:2603.01710.</li>
+<li>Trautmann, D., Ostapuk, N., Grail, Q., Pol, A., Bonifazi, G., Gao, S., &amp; Gajek, M. (2024, November). Measuring the groundedness of legal question-answering systems. In Proceedings of the Natural Legal Language Processing Workshop 2024 (pp. 176-186).</li>
+<li>Gao, T., Yen, H., Yu, J., &amp; Chen, D. (2023, December). Enabling large language models to generate text with citations. In Proceedings of the 2023 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (pp. 6465-6488).</li>
